-- title:
--   Monotonicity of the zero-scheme ideal under module maps
-- statement:
--   Let $X$ be a scheme and let $M$, $M'$ be objects of the category `X.Modules` of sheaves of $\mathcal O_X$-modules, regarded with its monoidal structure whose unit $\mathbb 1_{X.\mathrm{Modules}}$ is the structure sheaf. Let $s : \mathbb 1_{X.\mathrm{Modules}} \to M$ be a global section of $M$, i.e. a morphism out of the unit object, and let $f : M \to M'$ be a morphism of modules. For a section $t$ of a module and an open $U \subseteq X$, the coefficient ideal `coeffIdeal t U` is the ideal of $\Gamma(X,U)$ generated by the range of the coefficient map `coeff t U`, which assigns to a morphism $\varphi$ from the restriction of the module along $U \hookrightarrow X$ to the unit object of $U.\mathrm{Modules}$ an element of $\Gamma(X,U)$; and `zeroSchemeIdeal t` is the infimum, in the lattice `X.IdealSheafData`, of those ideal sheaf data $J$ with `coeffIdeal t U` $\le$ $J$-ideal at $U$ for every affine open $U$ of $X$. The assertion is that the zero-scheme ideal of the composite $s$ followed by $f$ is $\le$ the zero-scheme ideal of $s$ in `X.IdealSheafData`; equivalently, the closed subscheme cut out by $f \circ s$ contains that cut out by $s$. No quasi-coherence, invertibility or finiteness hypotheses are imposed on $M$, $M'$ or $f$.
--
--   This is the functoriality (monotonicity) of the vanishing scheme of a section in the module variable: if a section vanishes, so does its image under any module homomorphism. It is used in the comparison [`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.zeroSchemeIdeal_comp_eq_of_isIso`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.zeroSchemeIdeal_comp_eq_of_isIso), where equality is obtained for $f$ an isomorphism by applying the inequality in both directions.
